&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Manager, Field Marketing to join our Field Marketing &amp;amp; Advocacy team. This role owns how Addepar shows up at events across the globe — from national industry conferences and trade shows to our annual user conference, executive summits, and regional community programs. You will support the strategy, lead the team, and ensure every program Addepar runs delivers measurable brand and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage a team of three: two Field Marketing Managers focused on industry events and regional activations, and a Strategic Events Program Manager who owns our client event programs. Your job is to ensure the team is aligned, the portfolio is coherent, and that every event has a clear strategic purpose and is executed at the highest level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate at the intersection of business strategy, content, and event experience. You will partner closely with GTM, Product Marketing, R&amp;amp;D and executive leadership to ensure events drive awareness, deepen client relationships, accelerate pipeline, and reinforce Addepar’s position as a market leader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States for any employer without requiring current or future visa sponsorship (for example, employment-based visas such as H-1B, F-1/OPT, or similar), and must be authorized to begin work in the U.S. on their first day of employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of three field marketers — setting clear goals, maintaining high standards, and creating an environment where the team does their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish &amp;amp; reinforce roles, responsibilities, and success metrics for each team member, ensuring accountability against event targets, deadlines, and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Events Strategy + Annual Conference Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Addepar’s global events portfolio — providing your expert opinion on which events and programs to invest in, how to allocate team and budget resources, and how the full calendar connects to GTM priorities and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align the events calendar to territory priorities, pipeline goals, product launches, and campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end execution of our annual user conference, AddeConf, including agenda setting, content creation, event design, logistical oversight and pre- and post-event activation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate the events portfolio — cutting what’s underperforming, doubling down on what works, and identifying new opportunities as the business grows globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Alignment &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the point of contact across the organization for all things events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across internal stakeholders before, during, and after each program: ensuring Sales knows their role, Product Marketing’s messaging is reflected, and AM teams are briefed on their accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Measurement &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the events analytics function — building and maintaining a performance dashboard that tracks KPIs across all programs: leads generated, pipeline influenced, meetings held, cost per lead, NPS, and ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a culture of data-informed decision-making within the team, using post-event insights to continually improve strategy and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full Field Marketing events budget — including allocation across programs, spend tracking, and accountability for ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team maintains operational excellence across procurement, vendor contracts, invoicing, compliance submissions, and lead capture processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to key events domestically and occasionally internationally to support the team and maintain visibility with clients, partners, and internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
