&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addepar is looking for a Sr. Manager, Talent Acquisition to lead our APAC recruiting function from our Pune, India office. This is a player-coach role: you will lead and develop a team of recruiters while also owning a portfolio of critical requisitions yourself, across our Go-to-Market (Sales &amp;amp; Services), R&amp;amp;D (Engineering, AI, Data, and Product), and G&amp;amp;A (Finance, Legal, People, IT) organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as the senior recruiting voice for the region, setting hiring strategy in partnership with regional and global leaders while staying close enough to the work to know exactly what&#39;s happening in the pipeline. You are comfortable operating in a matrix organization, balancing global talent acquisition standards with the realities of local markets, and you know how to translate broad company hiring goals into a concrete regional plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have legal authorization to work in the country where this role is based on the first day of employment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of recruiters across multiple functions, setting clear goals, providing regular feedback, and building a strong bench of recruiting talent in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally own and manage a portfolio of high-priority, senior, or complex requisitions end to end, from intake through offer and close, across GTM, R&amp;amp;D, and G&amp;amp;A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the APAC recruiting strategy in partnership with regional business leaders and global TA leadership, translating company-wide hiring goals into a regional plan that reflects local market realities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively in a matrix organization, balancing global process and standards with the needs of local hiring managers, functional leaders, and business units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with hiring managers and business leaders to understand their staffing needs, advise on hiring strategy, and build durable, trust-based relationships across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive workforce planning conversations with business and People leaders, helping them think ahead of open reqs rather than react to them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong point of view on how AI and modern recruiting tools (sourcing, screening, scheduling, and candidate engagement) can improve speed, quality, and consistency across the team, and lead adoption of new tools and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use recruiting metrics (time to fill, pipeline health, source effectiveness, offer acceptance, and more) to diagnose bottlenecks and drive continuous improvement across the funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a consistently excellent, high-touch candidate experience, and represent Addepar&#39;s employer brand across APAC markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on employment law, hiring practices, and market compensation trends across the APAC countries in scope, ensuring recruiting activities remain compliant and competitive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with University Recruiting and campus programs where relevant to build long-term talent pipelines in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
