&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10+ years of progressive talent acquisition experience, including at least 5-7 years directly managing and developing a team of recruiters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience recruiting across multiple functions (for example: GTM, R&amp;amp;D, and G&amp;amp;A/Corporate), not just a single specialty, with the range to flex between technical, commercial, and operational hiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a matrix or global organization, working across functional and geographic reporting lines and building consensus without formal authority over every stakeholder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine player-coach: equally comfortable setting strategy in the boardroom and getting into the details of a live requisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record using data and recruiting metrics to make decisions, tell a clear story to leadership, and hold the team accountable to outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI-enabled recruiting tools and modern sourcing technology (for example: AI sourcing/screening tools, conversational scheduling, or GenAI-assisted workflows), with an eye for what&#39;s genuinely useful versus hype&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with applicant tracking systems (Greenhouse preferred) and the broader recruiting tech stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with APAC talent markets and the employment landscape across the relevant countries in scope; working knowledge of local employment law and compliance considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior business leaders and adjust style across cultures and seniority levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience in Human Resources, Business, or a related field; MBA or relevant certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
