&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4 years of relevant experience, ideally in a fast-paced, growing global tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable making decisions independently and exhibit strong problem-solving in the moment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the sensitivity of confidential information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with HR systems, ideally Workday, and Google Suite.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have in-depth knowledge of Polish laws, guidelines, and compliance regulations relative to employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an interest in working with not only Poland, but other locations across EMEA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to prioritise your time and can handle multiple projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent Polish proficiency alongside fluent written and spoken English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a fast-paced environment and can stay organised without missing a small detail&lt;/li&gt;
