&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5+ years of experience in a relevant role and domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2+ years of people Team leader experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Finance, Business Administration, Commerce, Economics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Private equity / Alternatives investment process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the financial investment/advisory industry with strong knowledge of capital markets, middle/back-office operations systems, and preferably with experience dealing with Alternatives (Private/Draw-down) Funds reporting statements and data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of demonstrating excellent attention to detail, effective problem-solving skills, and an ability to thrive in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills for engaging clients, data providers, and internal stakeholders across Sales, Services, and R&amp;amp;D&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-motivated to take on responsibility, forward thinking and pragmatic, and possess a collaborative team-player mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical skills preferred in any or all of the following: Microsoft Excel, Google Suite, Atlassian Jira/Confluence, SQL, Salesforce, or other common financial services systems and applications&lt;/li&gt;
